# ADR required for architecture changes

When making architecture or cross-cutting changes, add or update an ADR in `docs/adr/` in the **same change**.

## Triggers (ADR required)

- Add/remove/rename a zone, or change path / `assetPrefix` / Storybook `base`
- Change home rewrite / routing strategy
- Change monorepo tooling or shared package boundaries
- Change Storybook hosting (dev vs static zone verification)
- Change root file allowlist

## Not required

- Bug fixes, copy, single-component UI without structural impact

## How

1. Copy `docs/adr/0000-template.md` → `docs/adr/NNNN-short-kebab-title.md` (next number)
2. Fill Context / Decision / Consequences / Alternatives
3. Status: `Accepted` for shipped decisions; mark old ADRs `Superseded` when replaced
4. Update the index in `docs/adr/README.md`

Never put ADR files at repo root or directly under `docs/` (only under `docs/adr/`).
